{"code":"import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _add_kernel(\n    x_ptr,\n    y_ptr,\n    out_ptr,\n    n_elements,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n    IS_BF16: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    s = x + y\n    if IS_BF16:\n        s = s.to(tl.bfloat16)\n    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, s, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\n    assert x.shape == y.shape\n    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\n    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 2048\n    is_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\n    grid = (triton.cdiv(n, BLOCK_SIZE),)\n    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE, IS_BF16=is_bf16)\n    return out\n","draft":"Hypothesis: small-shape latency is dominated by host launch overhead, not kernel work. Observed contradiction: 4099-elem BF16 candidate (1.10us) is slower than torch.compile (0.92us), while 1M-elem candidate (3.32us) is 3x faster. The kernel is correct; the gap is fixed per-launch cost. Fix: reduce host-side overhead by using a static grid tuple instead of a lambda, and a slightly larger block to reduce program count for mid sizes.","evaluation":{"checks_passed":28,"cooperative_queue":{"lock_file":"/data/home/chenyizhou/kernel-agent-repair-experiment-v1/gpu4.lock","pid":2336507,"scope":"serializes this project's workers only","wait_seconds":4.5727938413619995e-05},"gpu":"NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090","measurement_condition":"shared_observed","resource_audit":{"after":{"free_mib":24199,"observed_utc":"2026-10-15T12:20:02.162202+00:00","pids":[],"power_watts":23.22,"sm_clock_mhz":210,"used_mib":12,