launch cost. Fix: reduce host-side overhead by using a static grid tuple instead of a lambda, and a slightly larger block to reduce program count for mid sizes.\",\"plan\":\"Output shape equals input shape; both inputs contiguous so flat offset = linear index. For shape [4099]: coord (4098) -> offset 4098, mask true; coord (4099) -> offset 4099, mask false. Padded lanes load other=0.0, add in FP32, cast to input dtype. BLOCK_SIZE=2048 reduces grid for 4099 to 2 programs. Static grid tuple avoids lambda call overhead.\",\"code_lines\":[\"import torch\",\"import triton\",\"import triton.language as tl\",\"\",\"\",\"@triton.jit\",\"def _add_kernel(\",\"    x_ptr,\",\"    y_ptr,\",\"    out_ptr,\",\"    n_elements,\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\",\"    IS_BF16: tl.constexpr,\",\"):\", \"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\",\"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\",\"    mask = offsets < n_elements\",\"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\",\"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\",\"    s = x + y\",\"    if IS_BF16:\",\"        s = s.to(tl.bfloat16)\",\"    tl.store(out_ptr + offsets, s, mask=mask)\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\",\"    assert x.is_cuda and y.is_cuda\",\"    assert x.shape == y.shape\",\"    assert x.dtype in (torch.float32, torch.bfloat16)\",\"    assert x.is_contiguous() and y.is_contiguous()\",\"    out = torch.empty_like(x)\",\"    n = x.numel()\",\"    BLOCK_SIZE = 2048\",\"    is_bf16 = x.dtype == torch.bfloat16\",\"    grid = (triton.cdiv(n, BLOCK_SIZE),)\",\"    _add_kernel[grid](x, y, out, n, BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE, IS_BF16=is_bf16)\",\"    return out\"]}","request_id":"baseline-counterexample-r1","source_sha256":"d7a8e964f361a846cba51ea1bcccc07ffcd53aad73d9668ab44ee8f99284222e"}
